# Impulsionando reengineering

## Authority

Source of truth: `docs/reengineering/`.

Conflict order: accepted ADRs → `02-target-architecture/` → `STATUS.md` → observed evidence → legacy `docs/` / `mem/`.

Stakeholder vision is input only — never skips phase gates.

## Current authorization

Only **Phase 0** (containment + discovery) is authorized.

Do **not**: implement monorepo/Nest/Dokploy; rebuild VPS; change DNS/routing; migrate tenants; clean Docker/releases; change DB schema; start Phases 1–7; re-enable contained workflows without a recorded decision.

Do **not** treat Proposed ADRs as implementation license.

## Target stack (Proposed — see TARGET-STACK.md)

Intended: pnpm modular monolith — `platform-web` / `tenant-web` / `app-web` (TanStack Start) + NestJS/Fastify `api` + independent `worker`; managed Supabase; Dokploy+Traefik+Cloudflare; GHCR SHA images; adapter integrations; governed AI later.

Full detail: `docs/reengineering/02-target-architecture/TARGET-STACK.md`.

## Hard safety

No secrets in chat/docs/git. No prod writes as diagnostics. No workers during SSR-only probes. HTTP 200 ≠ release proof. Backup ≠ proven without restore. Tenant isolation needs allow **and** deny tests. Mark unproven claims UNKNOWN. Prefer paths, SHAs, service names, timestamps as evidence.

## Working tree hazards

Do not stage/revert/regenerate `src/routeTree.gen.ts` without dedicated investigation + approval. Treat `src/generated/build-info.ts` as local build noise, not release identity.
